        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "APPEARANCES:\nMATTHEW S. HELLMAN, Washington, D.C.; on behalf\nof the Petitioner\nROBERT A. PARKER, Assistant to the Solicitor General,\nDepartment of Justice, Washington, D.C.; on\nbehalf of the Respondent\nHeritage Reporting Corporation"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Matthew S. Hellman",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1144",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a78e13823ade6eb5d662f4c01d7be1cbdc22f81ca1cee8912a11b9dba63a570f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a78e13823ade-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. HELLMAN: Thank you, Mr. Chief\nJustice, and may it please the Court:\nWhen Congress made it a felony to\nobstruct the due administration of the tax\ncode, it was not creating an all-purpose tax\ncrime; it was borrowing from a statute that\nprohibited the obstruction of a pending\nproceeding."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Matthew S. Hellman",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1144",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a78e13823ade6eb5d662f4c01d7be1cbdc22f81ca1cee8912a11b9dba63a570f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a78e13823ade-0000-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. HELLMAN: Certainly. There's a\nwhole range because obstruction, on their\ndefinition, is so broad. For example, you\ncould imagine a situation -- I'll take an\neveryday taxpayer, someone who pays their\ngardener, say, in cash, which is one of the\npredicate acts in this case as well."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1144",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a78e13823ade6eb5d662f4c01d7be1cbdc22f81ca1cee8912a11b9dba63a570f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a78e13823ade-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: There -- there is something to be done about the context that this was drafted in. As I look at the first half of this statute -\u00ad"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1144",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a78e13823ade6eb5d662f4c01d7be1cbdc22f81ca1cee8912a11b9dba63a570f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a78e13823ade-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: Well, does it get us part of the way there, though? Because the officer clause, as Justice Sotomayor suggests, you have to actually hinder something the officer is doing."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1144",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a78e13823ade6eb5d662f4c01d7be1cbdc22f81ca1cee8912a11b9dba63a570f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a78e13823ade-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: But doesn't everybody know -- doesn't everybody know when they're given an offer like this, you know, I'd rather"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1144",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a78e13823ade6eb5d662f4c01d7be1cbdc22f81ca1cee8912a11b9dba63a570f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a78e13823ade-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: Can -- can I go back to the question of -- of -- of the Department's prosecution policy?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1144",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "a78e13823ade6eb5d662f4c01d7be1cbdc22f81ca1cee8912a11b9dba63a570f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a78e13823ade-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 69,
        "start": 69
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If -- if so, I think you're suggesting work with the word in the statute, \"administration.\" That's the word?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1144",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "a78e13823ade6eb5d662f4c01d7be1cbdc22f81ca1cee8912a11b9dba63a570f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a78e13823ade-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 69,
        "start": 69
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And you think it's preferable given its heritage and for other reasons?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Hellman",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1144",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "a78e13823ade6eb5d662f4c01d7be1cbdc22f81ca1cee8912a11b9dba63a570f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a78e13823ade-0003-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 70,
        "start": 70
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "and if you look at the jury instructions in cases that have interpreted other obstruction statutes that apply to proceedings, which is never a defined term in those statutes, I don't have a case name for you, you'll see that they start to look like things like an audit where you have an individualized assessment or enforcement of some obligation enforceable by a subpoena power."
    },
    {
